{
  "_readme": [
    "THE ROWS THIS WAVE STOPPED SHIPPING — frozen, so the retirement migration can match on BYTES.",
    "",
    "Task 12 replaced fourteen standalone presets, six theme-family rows and one shelf row with five",
    "coordinated families of five content kinds. Seeds insert BY NAME and only when absent, so an",
    "existing install keeps every old row and gains the new ones on top.",
    "`ensure_retired_presets_are_gone` removes a row only when its name is here AND its",
    "`region_config_json` and `style_json` still equal the bytes below AND nothing points at it. A",
    "single edited colour makes the row somebody's work, and somebody's work is not a leftover.",
    "",
    "`layout` and `style` are STRINGS, not nested objects, and that is load-bearing. The comparison is",
    "byte-for-byte against what the seed wrote; parsing and re-serialising sorts the keys (serde_json's",
    "map is a BTreeMap) and would produce a string that equals nothing in any database. The shelf row's",
    "bytes are already key-sorted because the seed itself writes them through `Value::to_string()` —",
    "these are the bytes as inserted, not as authored.",
    "",
    "TWENTY-ONE ROWS, IN THREE GROUPS, and the groups are why the list is exactly this long:",
    "",
    "  · FOURTEEN standalone presets (`Midnight Blue` … `Lobby Sunrise`). `preset_templates()` is now",
    "    empty. Note `Lower Third Light`: the plan's list said thirteen and omitted it, which would",
    "    have stranded it in every existing install with nothing left that names it.",
    "  · SIX theme-family rows. The old four-kind families had a `Lower Third` member that the new",
    "    five-kind families do not (`Lower Third` is now a family of its own, not a kind), and the",
    "    Nocturne family is not one of the five, so all four of its rows go. Recovered from the",
    "    pre-change `theme_templates()` and verified byte-for-byte against it.",
    "  · ONE shelf row, `Lower Third · Scripture`, forced out because the new keyed family takes that",
    "    exact name and a seed that inserts by name cannot hold both.",
    "",
    "THAT ONE SHARED NAME HAS A PERMANENT CONSEQUENCE, and it is written here because it is neither",
    "reversible nor visible. Where the old shelf row is IN USE or was EDITED, the migration correctly",
    "keeps it, and `ensure_preset_templates` inserts by name only when ABSENT, so the keyed family",
    "member of that name is not installed on that boot. The name never becomes absent, so it is not",
    "installed on any later boot either: that church has a Lower Third family of FOUR, for good. Both",
    "halves are deliberate (a row somebody uses is never deleted, and a seed never overwrites a name",
    "that is taken), so it is a consequence and not a bug. Relay says so once per boot on stderr, and",
    "`ensure_retired_presets_are_gone` carries the same note.",
    "",
    "Nothing else is retired. Every other name the old seed shipped is still shipped, with unchanged",
    "bytes, so retiring it would delete a row the very next boot re-inserts under a NEW id — repointing",
    "whatever channel or plan cue pointed at it. That is the failure this list's length is guarding."
  ],
